# Rank 1002 / CVE-2020-35902: actix-codec's Framed carried a blanket
# impl<T, U> Unpin regardless of T while pinning its io field with
# Pin::new_unchecked. The blanket impl lets safe code move the value out of a
# Pin, and new_unchecked is the promise that it never moves; together a caller
# can free a buffer the pinned I/O object still reads.

test "rank1002: unconditional generic Unpin impl beside Pin::new_unchecked"
  lang rust
  expect VYQL-RACE-003
  code
  ```
  pub struct Framed<T, U> {
      io: T,
      codec: U,
      read_buf: BytesMut,
  }

  impl<T, U> Unpin for Framed<T, U> {}

  impl<T, U> Framed<T, U>
  where
      T: AsyncRead,
      U: Decoder,
  {
      pub fn next_item(&mut self, cx: &mut Context<'_>) -> Poll<Option<Result<U::Item, U::Error>>> {
          unsafe { Pin::new_unchecked(&mut self.io).poll_read_buf(cx, &mut self.read_buf) }
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1002: a bounded Unpin impl is conditional and sound"
  lang rust
  reject VYQL-RACE-003
  code
  ```
  pub struct Framed<T, U> {
      io: T,
      codec: U,
      read_buf: BytesMut,
  }

  impl<T: Unpin, U> Unpin for Framed<T, U> {}

  impl<T, U> Framed<T, U>
  where
      T: AsyncRead,
      U: Decoder,
  {
      pub fn next_item(&mut self, cx: &mut Context<'_>) -> Poll<Option<Result<U::Item, U::Error>>> {
          unsafe { Pin::new_unchecked(&mut self.io).poll_read_buf(cx, &mut self.read_buf) }
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1002: an unconditional Unpin impl with no unchecked pinning is fine"
  lang rust
  reject VYQL-RACE-003
  code
  ```
  pub struct Wrapper<T> {
      inner: Box<T>,
  }

  impl<T> Unpin for Wrapper<T> {}

  impl<T> Wrapper<T> {
      pub fn get(&self) -> &T {
          &self.inner
      }
  }
  ```
